 INPUT CARD>! Single point at the NSERCH=0 equilibrium-search starting geometry from        
 INPUT CARD>! caa005bIRCCML1stdef2TZVPP / ...TZVPPa / ...TZVPPb.                            
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! Purpose: caa005bIRCCML1stdef2TZVPPb (analytic gradient AND analytic Hessian,  
 INPUT CARD>! no numerical differentiation anywhere) still showed the same runaway pattern  
 INPUT CARD>! as the earlier SEMINUM runs -- energy dropping far faster than the ~0.1 A     
 INPUT CARD>! of nuclear motion could account for, and the approximate Hessian's leading    
 INPUT CARD>! curvature eigenvalue growing steadily more negative (-14.7 -> -33.0 across    
 INPUT CARD>! 4 steps). That rules out numerical noise as the cause. This test checks the   
 INPUT CARD>! remaining hypothesis directly: does a genuine lower-energy solution exist     
 INPUT CARD>! that the closed-shell RHF/RKS reference cannot represent?                     
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! Method: run UHF with alpha/beta symmetry deliberately broken via              
 INPUT CARD>! $GUESS MIX=.TRUE. (mixes HOMO/LUMO before the first SCF cycle so UHF does     
 INPUT CARD>! not just reconverge back to the RHF solution). Same charge/multiplicity       
 INPUT CARD>! (neutral singlet) as the RHF run -- this is an open-shell-singlet /           
 INPUT CARD>! broken-symmetry test, not a change of spin state.                             
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! Reference value to compare against:                                           
 INPUT CARD>! RHF/wB97X-D energy at this exact geometry = -491.6712565 (from                
 INPUT CARD>! caa005bIRCCML1stdef2TZVPPb, NSERCH=0). If UHF converges to something          
 INPUT CARD>! meaningfully lower than this, that confirms an RHF instability.               
